cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: >-
  Learning to decode correlated quantum errors: a topological graph neural
  decoder that surpasses minimum-weight matching under structured circuit-level
  noise
authors:
  - family-names: Huynh
    given-names: Molena
    email: molena.huynh@jmp.com
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/thmolena/Topological-Graph-for-Decoding-in-QEC"
abstract: >-
  A learned surface-code decoder benchmarked head-to-head against MWPM and
  BP+OSD on identical Stim shots with paired statistics (Wilson intervals,
  McNemar exact tests, paired bootstrap). Under structured correlated
  circuit-level noise, where matching's independence assumption fails, the
  learned decoder cuts MWPM's logical error rate by 46.1% at distance 3 and
  recovers 74.5% of the gap to the model-aware BP+OSD ceiling without being
  given the noise model; under independent noise, where MWPM is provably
  maximum-likelihood, the learned decoder pays a finite-sample premium and
  does not match it at the released reproduce scale. Part of the
  "spectral-truncation operators" (SpecOps) research program.
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - surface code
  - graph neural network
  - decoder
  - spectral-truncation operators
